A||||18||My7Fieros||Another question for the computer people in here...||||11||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||02-25-2001||08:34 PM||||Ive noticed that starting about 2 weeks ago or so, that my computer has been acting strange. Heres the skinny:<BR>Its an e-machines 400i. 400mghz, 56k blah blah blah. For about the past couple of weeks, its been doing some strange things..like going VERY slow (my 100 mghz 5 year old laptop is 10 times faster right now)..not only does it take FOREVER to bring up a website (or anything for that matter), but when I either log off or minimize whatever Im on..windows desktop comes back in stages so to speak....top portion................middle portion.................bottom...get it? instead of one quick motion like its always done. <BR>Also, I CONSTANLY get that stupid error message box w/ the red "X" that says something to the effect of "this program has performed an illeagle operation and will be closed down" message, w/ whatever application I was using at the top of the message (ie AOL, NAPSTER, ATI PLAYER, whatever).....<BR>As if that werent enough, its now doing this thing where it'll decide it wants to log onto AOL for no reason...ive woken up in the morning to see the AOL start up screen on with a little box w/ the ! simble saying "please enter a password"....WTF? Also, as I type this (on my old laptop), my computer has been autmatically defragging the c-drive.....FOR THE PAST 24 HOURS!!! It usually only takes around 2 hours at most..what gives? It goes 1%....2%....0%...(sometimes getting up to 4% before going back to zero). Ive always been good about "deleating the temp folders" and "deleating history"...hmmm<P>I just bought and installed a McAffe Virus Scan disk, and it shows all to be ok. <BR>I <B>REALLY REALLY</B> dont wont to have to run my recovery disk...Ive got alot of stuff that I dont want to lose......anybody have any thoughts? Ive got an extended warrenty on it, so it may just have to go to Best Buy, where they say that on alot of e-machines, instead of fixing they'll just replace it w/ what theyve got in stock closest to what is brought in (in my case, they dont make the 400i anymore, so Id more than likely get a 633  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )...but anyway, any ideas? Thanx.<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000001||Jake_Dragon||02-25-2001||09:18 PM||||You didn’t state is this 98 or ME?<BR>When was the last time you ran scandisk and defragged your hard drive?<BR>Look in device manager and see if you have any problems listed.<BR>If you find any devices listed with a yellow or red circle look and see what it says the problem could be.<BR>What were the last 5 programs you installed?<BR>Post what you find and I will do my best to help<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||02-25-2001||09:46 PM||||Oh sorry...its Windows 98...<BR>I checked under Device Manager, and there are no yellow or red circles.<BR>I check for errors about once a week, and the computer is automatically set up to run a defrag...either once a week or once a month I forget.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jake_Dragon||02-25-2001||10:07 PM||||Ok run msconfig.exe and look at what is running under startup.<BR>Uncheck all but:<BR>ScanRegistry<BR>SystemTray<BR>TaskMonitor<BR>LoadPowerProfile<P>Restart your PC and see if your problems are still present.<BR>If that corrects your problems than run msconfig again and enable one startup item and reboot<BR>Test to see if it is causing any problems. <BR>Repeat till you find the program that is causing your problems or run out of disabled items.<P>Post back if this doesn’t solve your problems.<BR>||||reg||2
Z||000004||Tweek||02-25-2001||10:20 PM||||When you are defragmenting your HD, you may want to do this... First do ctrl+alt+del and individuly end task on all the programs exect Explorer and Systray. then do a scandisk. Close that, check for any other running programs again making sure only those 2 are there. then do a defrag. dont do anything on your puter while its defragging or it will start over. PITA I know, but works better.<BR>Definatly run MSCONFIG and clean out unnessary stuff in the startup tab.<BR>But Im guessing your problems are deeper than this... I would put my money on the cooling system I.E... make sure the fan works.. cause when that goes, lotsa weird stuff happens.<BR>I dont want to say that you made a bad choice of computer brand, cause you can make a puter work if you wanna....  But Im sure youre familiar with buying Rebuilt Auto parts.. water pump, starter etc.. emachines are generally full of such parts. There is a reason that they only give you a 15 day warrenty.<P>Good Luck!<P>-Ted||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tweek||02-25-2001||10:22 PM||||OOPS.. sorry I forgot you said you had an extended warrenty...   Good for you!!  =)||||reg||1
Z||000006||RNGCRSH||02-25-2001||11:01 PM||||It sounds like you have a backdoor orifice type of virus if your computer is trying to establish an internet conection buy itself. also any program that changes a file will cause defrag to restart. Try and shut down all progs not needed from the CTRL+ALT+DEL menu then try a defrag if it works then its a program you have loaded if not make sure you have the latest Virus protection updates. Know this no virus software is 100% effective you should also try another, like norton or one of the shareware ones.<P>hope any of this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000007||ray b||02-26-2001||12:35 AM||||is your hard drive full or nearly full.that will slow it way down.||||reg||1
Z||000008||My7Fieros||02-26-2001||12:40 AM||||Hard drive is about 1/2 full (4.36 GB hard drive)...Ok Im gonna try everything that was mentioned...thanx. One thing did really get my attention though...someone said something about the "cooling system"...making sure the fan(s) are working properly. For the past few months, my comp has sounded like a dog w/ dry heaves....VERY loud at times, and obviously, VERY annoying! I just took apart the tower, pulled out the fans (2) and noticed SO much dust it was literally falling off in chunks! I went and bought a large can of that compressed air or whatever, and proceeded to BLAST everybit of dust and dirt and ...eh hem, dog hair out of the fans and the entire computer. After a thorough cleaning, Im back on it now, and it seems to be doing MUCH better...only time will tell though, so I'll reply in a day or two and let you know if this was the root of the probs..if not, I'm gonna try doing all the other things mentioned on here. Thanx! M7F<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 02-26-2001).]||||reg||1
