Z||000010||overlord||02-26-2001||01:07 AM||||if all else fails that is.<BR>My cousins comp was like that, error messages left and right, slow. I  couldnt take it so i reisnatlled windows for him. Nice and fresh, purrs nicely now.<P>Do you install a lot of programs, download a lot of things? Cuase that will do it.(mess up windows that is).<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||02-26-2001||03:14 AM||||IE shut down halfway thru the first time I replied to this, kind of ironic...<P>My computer's doing the same things, with a couple of exceptions (aol dialer etc) Run msconfig to try and locate the offending program.. that should work, but if you do have some sort of trojan virus etc, you might want to get a firewall. <A HREF="http://www.zonelabs.com" TARGET=_blank>www.zonelabs.com</A>  has a program called ZoneAlarm. it's free for non-commercial use and works very well. This will alert you if someone is trying to use your computer remotely. As for the defrag restarting, you should check to make sure that a screensaver or some form of power saving feature isn't kicking in. Disable all these and run a full surface scan and defrag. But overall, nothing works as well as a full system reinstall. You should find a friend with a CD burner etc to back up your files first, either that or install a 2nd hard drive to put the files on. (if you're not a techie you might want to get a professional to do that because you need to change jumper switches etc)<P>If your fans are still making any funny noises, get them replaced. An overheated CPU is as bad as an overheated engine.. think of a CPU as an aircooled engine that's in a sealed box, and the only airflow is with a few small fans. If those fans break, there's no airflow, heat builds up, and the system starts crashing randomly and it could result in data loss eventually, not to mention a crispy processor.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000012||Standard||02-26-2001||01:07 PM||||Yep, broken fan is a bad bad thing..  not as much a problem with a 400 mhz chip but still not good.<P>Somebody tested to see how long an AMD Thunderbird 1 Ghz chip would last without a fan and heatsink.  It toasted itself in <B>7</B> seconds!||||reg||1
Z||000013||Tigger||02-26-2001||01:21 PM||||I can believe it, that's the cpu I have in mine.  Recently added another case fan for it just in case.<P>1 CPU fan w/ funky spiral alum. heat sink.<BR>2 Case fans<BR>1 PWR supply fan<BR>1 Fan on video card.<P>I got lots of fans.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">  Still very quiet considering.<P>My7, just disable McAfee when you defrag and make sure you don't have a screensaver running.  Just turn off the monitor if you're worried about burning anything into it.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Wade87GT||02-27-2001||10:44 PM||||My7Fieros,<P>Alot of applications today continually report back to the "home office" as they monitor your surf habits, all for "marketing" purposes. Examples are Realaudio/Player/Download,MyCometCursor, any of those browser skins, that purple gorilla, etc. When you close out your browser, these applications try to stay open and ready for their next attempt. Sometimes they'll relaunch your browser. McAfee is notorious for crashing Win98. Its default setting tries to scan the floppy upon logoff or shut down. No floppy installed, it can crash or hang. Also, alot of websites are flooding the net with poorly written Java scripts that can overwhelm your RAM. Bottom line: The internet has gotten to big for its own good. If you can't find all the little problems, the last choice is to reformat and re-install. And try to stay away from all the gee-wiz stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Bugsy||02-28-2001||11:24 AM||||Ironic, my system totally crashed the day before this thread started, I still don't know exactly what happened but it affected the boot secters of both drives and i had to flash out the bios just to get one of the drives to take a fresh install. <P>------------------<BR>86 SE I'm addicted and proud of it<BR>Kevin||||reg||9
Z||000016||My7Fieros||02-28-2001||02:36 PM||||<B>WADE87GT</B>....man I tell you what, you mentioned something that I never thought of.....my problems actually started right <B>after</B> I downloaded that stupid purple monkey thing that talks to you!!! INTERESTING. I finally uninstalled him, but it was a <B>MAJOR</B> pain in the a$$!! I still am not positive its completely out of my computer. Alot of what you said makes sense to.....hmmm....<BR>At any rate, after a thourough cleaning of the fans and internal components, I havent had any of the above problems....w/ the exception that its still alittle slower than usual, but not <I>too</I> bad. It also runs alot quieter. Another thing I started doing is turning the computer off at night, or whenever I leave for a while. Ive always just left my computer on...maybe turning it off for the night about once a month or so...this should help it stay cleaner and cooler....Im going to Best Buy and am going to buy another fan or two...<BR>I also plan on "upping" the memory to, its only 32mb or ram (zzzzz). Anyway thanx again.<BR>M7F||||reg||4
Z||000017||Wade87GT||02-28-2001||04:22 PM||||That purple monkey is really persistant, you may have to go into the Registry to get rid of it all. The Registry is not a place for the average user to tread, so be careful if you do.<P>Wade||||reg||14
Z||000018||Raydar||02-28-2001||04:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B>[b]<BR>I also plan on "upping" the memory to, its only 32mb or ram (zzzzz). Anyway thanx again.<BR>M7F</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>When I increased my RAM from 32mb to 64, it made a tremendous difference in how my 'puter behaved. <P>BTW... I don't know about the purple monkey, but I've seen a browser that just beats the hell out of our network at work. It's called "NeoPlanet". Was transmitting (blocked) requests to our firewall at the rate of about 100 per second!!! Couldn't find any way to disable the flood, either. Had to kill the app.<BR>Just a handful of workstations were causing  really ugly things to happen.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
